    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (87.42) headlining the lineup as the clear strongest play. Facing Cal Quantrill, **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from a high-efficiency matchup against a pitcher with a 4.79 xERA, combined with an elite 0.469 xwOBA that cements his status as an anchor. Alongside him, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.12) is a mandatory start; his elite sprint speed addresses our critical need for stolen bases, and his 14% platoon edge against Hunter Greene makes him one of the highest-upside plays on the board. **Trea Turner** (68.35) and **Junior Caminero** (67.34) also provide excellent stability at the top of the order, taking advantage of favorable lineup positioning to drive scoring potential in a competitive 5x5 environment.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Casey Schmitt** (53.08), who narrowly missed the cut behind **Luke Raley** (54.62). While **Casey Schmitt** offered a slight wind-aided advantage and a favorable platoon profile against Tanner Gordon, the optimizer favored **Luke Raley** due to the superior matchup against Nick Martinez and a strong 19% SP skill adjustment. Elsewhere, we are exercising caution with **Christian Yelich** (54.09); while he remains in the lineup, his low score is suppressed by a harsh -19% SP skill penalty against Braxton Ashcraft. Managers should note that **Carson Benge** and **Caleb Durbin** were excluded not just for lower scores, but due to a 38% rain risk that introduces unnecessary volatility. We will continue to monitor the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Dillon Dingler**, **Colt Keith**, and **Pedro Ramirez**, as any unexpected shift in batting order could further impact their marginal efficiency scores today.",
